pedopilot: third-party data and models
=====================================

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the code only. The data table and the model weights below come from
third parties under their own terms. Check those terms before redistributing them or using them
commercially.

1. data_snapshot/conus_0_30.parquet (NOT included in this repository)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
The exact table every published run used (28,192 soil profiles, conterminous USA, 0-30 cm). It is not
distributed here because of the terms below; see data_snapshot/README.md.
sha256 7a890cb6be3d858894c48cd48c9c28c45aedeec42f335a278c9d42a4473ee624 (checked by the code; also in
src/pedopilot/paths.py). Built with `python -m pedopilot prep` (src/pedopilot/data.py) and added to the
repository on 2026-09-27.

Derived from:
* WoSIS "latest" (ISRIC - World Soil Information), downloaded from the ISRIC WFS before the snapshot date:
  layers clay, orgc, phaq, nitkjd, cecph7 and tceq, aggregated to 0-30 cm per profile. WoSIS data carry
  the licence of each source dataset. Source datasets in the table (column dataset_id): US-NCSS (27,878
  profiles), WD-WISE (291), WD-ISIS (20), CA-CanSIS (2), MX-INEGI (1). ISRIC documents the licence of
  each source dataset (mostly CC BY or CC BY-NC): verify it for each dataset above.
  Reference: Batjes, N. H., Calisto, L. and de Sousa, L. M. (2024). Providing quality-assessed and
  standardised soil data to support global mapping and modelling (WoSIS snapshot 2023). Earth System
  Science Data 16, 4735-4765.
* WorldClim 2.1 (Fick and Hijmans 2017): the 19 bioclimatic variables (5 arc-minutes) and elevation
  (2.5 arc-minutes), sampled at the profile locations (columns bio1-bio19, elev, slope, relief). Check
  the terms of use on worldclim.org before redistributing values derived from WorldClim.
  Reference: Fick, S. E. and Hijmans, R. J. (2017). WorldClim 2: new 1-km spatial resolution climate
  surfaces for global land areas. International Journal of Climatology 37, 4302-4315.

WorldClim 2.1 terms (worldclim.org, checked 2026-09-30): "freely available for academic use and other
non-commercial use. Redistribution or commercial use is not allowed without prior permission." They do not say
whether point values extracted from the grids count as redistribution, and WoSIS source datasets other than
US-NCSS (314 profiles) may carry non-commercial terms. The table is therefore kept out of the public
repository. Anyone can rebuild an equivalent table with `download` and `prep` (a rebuilt table differs from the
snapshot because WoSIS "latest" changes over time), and the exact table can be shared with researchers on
request, subject to these terms.

2. TabICLv2 regressor checkpoint (models/tabicl-regressor-v2-20260212.ckpt)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Downloaded by `python -m pedopilot download --tabicl-only` from huggingface.co/jingang/TabICL, or by
the tabicl package at first use; not included in the repository. TabICL (Inria SODA team): the tabicl
code is released under the BSD-3-Clause licence (package metadata), and the Hugging Face model
repository jingang/TabICL is tagged BSD-3-Clause (checked 2026-09-30; re-check the model card before
redistributing the weights).

3. Python packages
------------------
The code depends on packages under their own licences, among them tabicl 2.2.0 (BSD-3-Clause) and
tabm 0.0.3 (Yandex Research; Apache-2.0), as stated in their package metadata. Nothing from them is
included in this repository.
